Lab 1: Install Private Automation Hub
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Install and configure the Private Automation Hub on a Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) server
Verify the installation through the web interface
Connect the Private Automation Hub to the Automation Controller
Understand the role of Private Automation Hub in managing Ansible content collections
Configure basic authentication and user management for the hub
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with RHEL/CentOS system administration
Knowledge of Ansible fundamentals and collections
Understanding of web services and HTTP protocols
Basic networking concepts (ports, firewalls, DNS)
Technical Requirements:

RHEL 8 or 9 server with minimum 4GB RAM and 20GB disk space
Root or sudo access to the server
Internet connectivity for downloading packages
Web browser for accessing the hub interface
