Task 5: Connect Hub to Automation Controller
Subtask 5.1: Configure Authentication Token
First, create an API token for the Automation Controller to use:

In the Galaxy NG web interface, navigate to User Settings → API Tokens

Click Create Token and provide:

Name: automation-controller-token
Description: Token for Automation Controller integration
Copy the generated token (you'll need this for the controller configuration)

Subtask 5.2: Configure Automation Controller (Simulation)
Since this is a lab environment, we'll simulate the controller configuration. In a real environment, you would configure this in the Automation Controller web interface:

# Create a configuration file that shows how to connect to our hub
cat > /opt/automationhub/controller-config.yml << 'EOF'
# Automation Controller Configuration for Private Automation Hub
# This would be configured in the Automation Controller web interface

automation_hub_url: "http://your-server-ip/api/galaxy/"
automation_hub_auth_url: "http://your-server-ip/api/galaxy/v3/"
automation_hub_token: "your-api-token-here"
automation_hub_ssl_verify: false  # Set to true in production with proper SSL

# Collections configuration
collections:
  - name: community.general
    source: automation_hub
  - name: ansible.posix
    source: automation_hub
EOF

echo "Configuration file created at /opt/automationhub/controller-config.yml"
