Subtask 5.3: Test Collection Upload
Let's test uploading a collection to verify everything is working:

# Switch to automationhub user
sudo su - automationhub
source /opt/automationhub/venv/bin/activate

# Install ansible-core for collection management
pip install ansible-core

# Create a test namespace and collection
mkdir -p /tmp/test_collection/my_namespace/my_collection

# Create collection metadata
cat > /tmp/test_collection/my_namespace/my_collection/galaxy.yml << 'EOF'
namespace: my_namespace
name: my_collection
version: 1.0.0
description: Test collection for Private Automation Hub
authors:
  - Test Author <test@example.com>
license:
  - MIT
tags:
  - test
  - demo
dependencies: {}
EOF

# Create a simple module
mkdir -p /tmp/test_collection/my_namespace/my_collection/plugins/modules
cat > /tmp/test_collection/my_namespace/my_collection/plugins/modules/hello.py << 'EOF'
#!/usr/bin/python
from ansible.module_utils.basic import AnsibleModule

def main():
    module = AnsibleModule(
        argument_spec=dict(
            name=dict(type='str', default='World')
        )
    )
    
    name = module.params['name']
    result = dict(
        changed=False,
        message=f'Hello, {name}!'
    )
    
    module.exit_json(**result)

if __name__ == '__main__':
    main()
EOF

# Build the collection
cd /tmp/test_collection/my_namespace/my_collection
ansible-galaxy collection build

# The collection tarball will be created in the current directory
ls -la *.tar.gz
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Service Won't Start
If Galaxy NG service fails to start:

# Check service logs
sudo journalctl -u galaxy-ng -f

# Check if database is accessible
sudo -u automationhub psql -h localhost -U automationhub -d automationhub -c "SELECT 1;"

# Verify Redis is running
redis-cli ping
Issue 2: Web Interface Not Accessible
If you can't access the web interface:

# Check if services are running
sudo systemctl status nginx galaxy-ng

# Check if ports are open
sudo netstat -tlnp | grep -E ':(80|8080)'

# Check firewall rules
sudo firewall-cmd --list-all
Issue 3: Database Connection Issues
If there are database connection problems:

# Check PostgreSQL status
sudo systemctl status postgresql

# Verify database exists
sudo -u postgres psql -l | grep automationhub

# Test database connection
sudo -u automationhub psql -h localhost -U automationhub -d automationhub
Issue 4: Permission Errors
If you encounter permission errors:

# Fix ownership of automation hub files
sudo chown -R automationhub:automationhub /opt/automationhub

# Fix permissions for static files
sudo chmod -R 755 /opt/automationhub/static
sudo chmod -R 755 /opt/automationhub/media
